# Regression test for a cutback in ALagrange contact analysis.
# A cutback restores the contact state of the last converged increment, so the
# contact matrix structure has to be rebuilt from the restored state as well.
# The y displacement of UPPER is -1.0 in STEP1 (pressing) and +1.5 in STEP2
# (separating).  In STEP2 some slave nodes separate (Cont2Free), the matrix
# structure is rebuilt without them, and the Newton iteration then reaches
# MAXITER=10, so the increment is cut back.  Without the rebuild, the restored
# contact nodes are missing from the matrix structure and the analysis stops with
# "cannot find connectivity".
# A cutback while only pressing does not detect this, because the restored contact
# nodes are then a subset of the rebuilt structure.
# Whether a cutback follows a separation depends on the displacements, MAXITER and
# the initial time increments, so recheck the failure without the rebuild when
# changing them.  FRICTION_CONE=FROZEN for the same reason: with the cone following
# the normal force STEP2 converges in four increments and the only cutback left
# happens before any contact state change, which does not exercise the rebuild.
# STEP2 ends with all nodes separated, so the result does not depend on the
# frictional history and agrees between the parallel settings.
#  Control File for FISTR
## Analysis Control
!VERSION
 3
!SOLUTION, TYPE=NLSTATIC
!WRITE,RESULT
## Solver Control
### Boundary Condition
!BOUNDARY, GRPID=1
 ALL, 3, 3, 0.0
 BOTTOM, 2, 2, 0.0
 CENTER, 1, 1, 0.0
 UPPER,  2, 2, -1.0
!BOUNDARY, GRPID=2
 ALL, 3, 3, 0.0
 BOTTOM, 2, 2, 0.0
 CENTER, 1, 1, 0.0
 UPPER,  2, 2, 1.5
!CONTACT_ALGO, TYPE=ALAGRANGE, FRICTION_CONE=FROZEN
!CONTACT, GRPID=1,NPENALTY=100,TPENALTY=100
 CP1, 0.3, 1000
!AUTOINC_PARAM, NAME=AP1
 0.5, 20, 100, 10, 2
 1.75, 10,  50,  5, 2
 0.25,  5
### STEP
!STEP, SUBSTEPS=9999, CONVERG=1.0e-5, MAXITER=10, INC_TYPE=AUTO,AUTOINCPARAM=AP1,MAXRES=100
 1.0, 1.0, 1E-5, 1.0
 BOUNDARY, 1
 CONTACT,  1
!STEP, SUBSTEPS=9999, CONVERG=1.0e-5, MAXITER=10, INC_TYPE=AUTO,AUTOINCPARAM=AP1,MAXRES=100
 1.0, 1.0, 1E-5, 1.0
 BOUNDARY, 2
 CONTACT,  1
### Material
!MATERIAL, NAME=MAT1
!HYPERELASTIC, TYPE=MOONEY-RIVLIN
 0.1486, 0.4849, 0.0789
### Solver Setting
!SOLVER,METHOD=CG,PRECOND=1,ITERLOG=YES,TIMELOG=YES
 1000, 1
 1.0e-10, 1.0, 0.0
!END
